  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5243",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a complex relationship with LB2518-MEL through a series of target interactions. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for A704, which in turn is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and also targets Leukocyte common antigen, which is targeted by 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, ultimately leading to LB2518-MEL. This indicates that Mollicellin N may influence LB2518-MEL through multiple pathways, possibly through different molecular mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mollicellin N to modulate LB2518-MEL via distinct targets, suggesting a broader role in cellular signaling or metabolic regulation. The evidence supports a mechanism where Mollicellin N could act as a bridge or regulator, influencing LB2518-MEL through a chain of targets, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
